  "id": "jittering",
  "term": "jittering",
  "definition": "Jittering is the addition of small, rapid viewpoint shifts to a visual display, creating an optic flow that varies rather than remaining smooth. In this context, it is used in self-motion research because such visual jitter can strengthen the illusion of moving while the observer is actually still.",
